Subject: [PATCH] Add shared log for an auto-logging Claude Code plugin

app.py's Register tab now reads data/auto_log.jsonl (via the new
auto_log.py) and merges in "classified" entries, tagged
claude-code-auto, with a Refresh button to re-pull the file on demand.

This is the other half of genai-usage-logger, a Claude Code plugin
(hooks module, not part of this repo) that watches every prompt in a
session, logs it as pending, and classifies pending entries on its own
timer against the same five dimensions and validation rules as
classifier.py, duplicated there since the plugin's sandboxed
environment can't import this project's Python. The goal is to match
the thesis's "enterprise AI gateway" framing: nobody fills in a form,
the log is read automatically from what an employee actually typed.

data/auto_log.jsonl is gitignored since it holds raw prompt text before
classification.
